-- title:
--   Inverting F and t leaves the Abel fibre sum unchanged
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma$ be an arbitrary subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, let $F : \mathfrak{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ be an arbitrary function on the upper half-plane, and let $t \in \mathbb{C}$ with $t \neq 0$. For a function $G$ and a value $s$, [`ModularCurve.abelFibreSumOf`](def/ModularCurve_AbelFibreSumOf.html#L20) $\Gamma$ $G$ $s$ is the element of the dual space of $\mathrm{CuspForm}(\Gamma,2)$ given by the (finitely supported) sum, over the orbits $\xi$ of $\Gamma$ acting on $\mathfrak{H}$, of the scalar multiples $\bigl(m_G(s,\xi_{\mathrm{out}})/e(\xi_{\mathrm{out}})\bigr)\cdot \mathrm{per}_\Gamma(i,\xi_{\mathrm{out}})$, where $\xi_{\mathrm{out}}$ is a chosen representative of $\xi$; here $m_G(s,\tau)$ is `valueMultiplicity`, the natural number obtained from the meromorphic order at $\tau$ of $z \mapsto G(\mathrm{ofComplex}\,z) - s$ by discarding the value $\top$ and truncating at $0$, $e(\tau)$ is `orbifoldIndexOf`, the cardinality of the stabiliser of $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by $\Gamma$ and $-1$ divided (in $\mathbb{N}$) by $2$, and $\mathrm{per}_\Gamma(\tau_0,\tau_1)$ sends a weight-$2$ cusp form $f$ to $\int_0^1 \mathrm{periodIntegrandOf}\,\Gamma\,\tau_0\,\tau_1\,f$. The assertion is that the fibre sum attached to $\tau \mapsto (F\tau)^{-1}$ and to the value $t^{-1}$ coincides, as a linear functional, with the fibre sum attached to $F$ and to $t$.
--
--   The multiplicity with which a function attains a value is unchanged on passing to reciprocals, so the divisor-like data entering the Abel–Jacobi fibre sum at level $\Gamma$ are the same for $(F,t)$ and for $(1/F,1/t)$. The identity is used in the proof that the Abel–Jacobi image of such a fibre lies in the period lattice of $\Gamma$, where it permits a normalisation of the value $t$.
